    year = "2006",
    volume = "12",
    note = "CORE ARGUMENT: Discusses the political philosophy of the late Paul Natorp, asking whether it is utopian detachment from reality or perceptive critique of the present. RELEVANCE: Source for Natorp's political and social idealism in and after the First World War, the context in which Marburg neo-Kantians connected Kant's cosmopolitan writings to post-war international order. POSITION: Marburg political philosophy (Natorp).",
